# Project-Wide Preferences

Default rules that apply to all work in this workspace.

## 1. Internationalization (i18n) required

All user-facing UI text must use i18n keys — never hardcode strings in components.

- When adding a new key, update **every locale file** the project uses (`messages/*.json` or the project's locale convention) with the same key structure.
- If a locale file is missing a value, fill it temporarily with the English string to avoid build/runtime errors.
- Code, comments, and identifiers stay in English.

```typescript
// ❌ Bad
<Button>Save</Button>

// ✅ Good
<Button>{t('common.save')}</Button>
// + en.json: { "common": { "save": "Save" } }
// + es.json: { "common": { "save": "Guardar" } }
```

## 2. Agent responses in English

Explanations, summaries, step-by-step guidance, and conclusions are written in **English**.

Keep the following in their original form:

- Code identifiers, variable/function/class names, file paths, branch names
- Terminal commands, package/API names, config keys
- Error/log quotes, external doc and issue URLs
- Code comments (English by convention)

## 3. Commit / push policy — no automatic push

After completing work:

1. Run relevant lint / type-check / unit tests.
2. **Wait for explicit user instruction** before `git push`, regardless of test results.
3. Commit only when the user requests it; push requires a separate instruction.
4. If tests fail, report the failure and do not push.

Detailed policy (default mode/model, Plan→Auto Build flow, push exceptions) is in
[agent-default-workflow](agent-default-workflow.mdc).

> Force push to `main`/`master` or destructive commands without user request are
> prohibited per [git workflow rules](common-git-workflow.md).
